<section id="s-trick" data-code="trick">
<div class="section-no">04 — Key Trick</div>
<h2>Progressive and Truncated OPD in Action</h2>
<p>
  POPD avoids early exposure to unreliable feedback by beginning with short rollouts. TOPD leverages the observation that in reasoning tasks, the teacher’s core characteristics (e.g., logical steps) are often captured in the initial prefix of the rollout.
</p>
<p>
  Both methods reduce the length-dependent memory and computation costs approximately in proportion to the horizon length.
</p>

